## Final report template

Always end with this routing trace:

```markdown
## QA Orchestration Report

**Ticket:** DS-N — <title>
**Outcome:** <Success | Test issue (pending fix) | Application bug filed | Blocked>

### Routing trace
| Step | Handler | Result |
|------|---------|--------|
| 1. Analyze requirements | Coordinator | <brief> |
| 2. Test creation | test-writer | <spec paths / blocked dependencies> |
| 3. Spec review | Coordinator | <approved / gaps noted> |
| 4. Test execution | Coordinator | <pass \| fail — command run> |
| 5–6. Diagnosis | triage | <classification or N/A if green> |
| 7. Test fix proposal | Coordinator | <proposed fix or N/A> |
| 8–9. Jira filing | bug-reporter | <DS-XXX URL or awaiting confirmation> |

### Artifacts
| Type | Path |
|------|------|
| Spec | `tests/<file>.spec.ts` |
| Evidence / log | `ci-artifacts/run-<id>-failed.log` |
| Playwright report | `ci-artifacts/run-<id>/` |
| Jira | <URL or —> |
| Reliability | `eval-report.md` |

### Subagent reports
<Paste or summarize test-writer, triage, and bug-reporter reports>
```

## CI follow-up

When the user asks to continue through CI (or a PR check fails):

1. Resolve the failed GitHub Actions run (`.github/workflows/e2e.yml` or `.github/workflows/test-generation.yml` when that workflow exists).
2. Delegate to `triage` with run ID/URL — same gates as local failures.
3. Do not file Jira until steps 8–9 are satisfied.
4. Run `node .cursor/hooks/regenerate-eval-report.mjs` (same script as step 11 and the Cursor hooks).
